WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.499
What does three-machine agreement add, and what does it still not prove?

q0002
00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:15.917
This episode has one job: Three guarded Linux CPU runs reproduced the B2/B4 direction descriptively, but they do not become one pooled inferential interval or erase the local study's scope.

q0003
00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:25.335
We build on Corrected B2/B4 V3 kernel result; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:32.838
Replication checks whether a scoped direction appears again under separately recorded machines and runs.

q0005
00:00:32.838 --> 00:00:40.341
Watch for the label replication; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:40.341 --> 00:00:48.347
When we say descriptive machine result, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:57.357
The term within-run interval receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:03.856
We will keep between-machine variation visible whenever its definition controls the inference.

q0009
00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:12.866
The next sequence uses Shared Boolean expression as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0010
00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:16.853
Our stable example is Shared Boolean expression.

q0011
00:01:16.853 --> 00:01:26.271
S=A AND B; F=(S AND C AND D) OR (S AND E), with binary source syntax and stable variable order A,B,C,D,E.

q0012
00:01:26.271 --> 00:01:32.267
Carry AST, CSE, CSE-flat, CM-IR, lowering, and operation accounting across episodes.

q0013
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:39.770
We now construct the Shared Boolean expression and name every part before interpreting it.

q0014
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:48.780
Place the accepted local estimate and three pod estimates in separate machine columns with identical ratio labels.

q0015
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:56.283
Attempt and refuse an unjustified pooled interval, then state what direction replication does support.

q0016
00:01:56.283 --> 00:02:01.275
Now isolate three-pod descriptive replication inside Shared Boolean expression.

q0017
00:02:01.275 --> 00:02:10.285
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for three-pod descriptive replication changes.

q0018
00:02:10.285 --> 00:02:19.295
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to three-pod descriptive replication, not to a substituted workload.

q0019
00:02:19.295 --> 00:02:24.287
Four machine columns build independently from verified raw results.

q0020
00:02:24.287 --> 00:02:30.283
Now isolate local inference versus machine replication inside Shared Boolean expression.

q0021
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:39.701
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for local inference versus machine replication changes.

q0022
00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:49.119
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to local inference versus machine replication, not to a substituted workload.

q0023
00:02:49.119 --> 00:02:58.537
Across three guarded CPU pods, row-weighted bare CM/CSE-flat was 0.9026–0.9126 overall and 0.9746–0.9766 at k=16.

q0024
00:02:58.537 --> 00:03:05.538
Read that statement only within this scope: B2/B4 corrected three-pod CPU replication.

q0025
00:03:05.538 --> 00:03:11.032
Its declared measurement boundary is compiled evaluator kernel after compilation.

q0026
00:03:11.032 --> 00:03:18.535
The uncertainty field says descriptive across three machines; post-hoc per-pod formula intervals are separate.

q0027
00:03:18.535 --> 00:03:27.953
Every ratio must state numerator, denominator, workload, measurement boundary, and uncertainty; below one favors CM only for CM/comparator.

q0028
00:03:27.953 --> 00:03:33.447
Read that statement only within this scope: video evidence contract.

q0029
00:03:33.447 --> 00:03:37.936
Its declared measurement boundary is all numeric scenes.

q0030
00:03:37.936 --> 00:03:41.923
The uncertainty field says declared per ratio.

q0031
00:03:41.923 --> 00:03:51.341
The nearest confusing lesson is Truth digests, alternating schedules, clustering, and intervals; it owns truth-digest exactness, while this episode owns three-pod descriptive replication.

q0032
00:03:51.341 --> 00:04:00.759
Begin with A and B, compute the shared subexpression S once, and keep that identity color on every outgoing use.

q0033
00:04:00.759 --> 00:04:06.755
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate three-pod descriptive replication.

q0034
00:04:06.755 --> 00:04:16.173
The left branch combines S with C and D, while the right branch combines the same S with E.

q0035
00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:23.174
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate local inference versus machine replication.

q0036
00:04:23.174 --> 00:04:32.592
Both branches meet at the final OR, so the shared node changes program structure without changing the Boolean output.

q0037
00:04:32.592 --> 00:04:42.010
A raw syntax view may draw S twice; a shared graph draws one node with two outgoing edges.

q0038
00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:49.513
Lowering the graph assigns dependency-ordered slots, but slot numbers are not new Boolean operations.

q0039
00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:57.016
Instruction count, primitive execution count, live buffers, and packed storage therefore remain separate ledgers.

q0040
00:04:57.016 --> 00:05:06.434
Changing from bigint bits to word lanes changes storage and execution layout, not the meaning of S or F.

q0041
00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:13.937
The three pod values are descriptive; they are not a predeclared pooled confidence interval.

q0042
00:05:13.937 --> 00:05:21.440
Identify which uncertainty belongs within one run and which would require a between-machine design.

q0043
00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.432
Replication adds another scope; it does not erase scope.

q0044
00:05:26.432 --> 00:05:35.850
A common mistake is this: Three similar pod ratios can automatically be averaged into the local study's confidence interval.

q0045
00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:41.846
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: three-pod descriptive replication.

q0047
00:05:44.985 --> 00:05:53.493
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: Replication adds another scope; it does not erase scope.

q0048
00:05:53.493 --> 00:05:59.992
Repeated direction strengthens portability evidence without broadening the scientific claim for free.
